Step 7: Machine learning basics (from month 6, optional but recommended)

Since you already know Pandas and visualisation, adding basic ML is a short step and supports both your
backup role and your AI project. Learn: train and test split, linear and logistic regression, decision trees,
random forest, KMeans clustering, evaluation metrics (accuracy, precision, recall, F1, confusion matrix),
and overfitting. Use the Scikit Learn library.

• Learn: Kaggle Learn courses (kaggle.com/learn), free and hands on. The Scikit Learn official user
guide for reference.
• Practise: Kaggle datasets and beginner competitions such as Titanic.
• Then: learn how LLM based apps work: embeddings, vector search, and RAG. Hugging Face
(huggingface.co) has free courses and models.
